  "key_finding": "Calendar-based bear year detection (_bear_years) is too coarse. BTC 1mo return is a much better regime signal. When BTC monthly return is < -5%, suppressing longs avoids losers across ALL years, not just bear years. This is a universal improvement, not just a bear market fix.",
  "recommended_implementation": {
    "code_change": "After the BTC regime block (~line 409), add: _deep_bear = np.nan_to_num(_m_ret_1mo_h, nan=0) < -0.05; long_signal[_deep_bear] = False",
    "mechanism": "Uses existing _m_ret_1mo_h (BTC monthly return) already computed for the short gate. When BTC had a >5% down month, longs are suppressed. This is NOT a calendar check — it fires dynamically based on actual regime.",
    "why_it_works": "Longs entered after BTC drops >5% in a month are statistically losers across all market phases. The positioning signal (contrarian OI/flow) suggests buying the dip, but in real bear months these dips keep dipping.",
    "variant_choice": "A4 (-5% threshold) for max total return, A5 (-10%) for lower drawdown. Both are strong."
